.TH SLOW_CONTROL_SUMMARY.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "otsdaq-mu2e-calorimeter 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
slow_control_summary.sh \- collect the latest calorimeter slow-control reading of every board
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slow_control_summary.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slow_control_summary.sh
summarises the per-board slow-control logs that the
.B ROC Slow Control
FE macro of the
.B ROCCalorimeterInterface
otsdaq plugin writes.
Each invocation of that macro appends one timestamped line per board to
.IR slowControl NNN .log
and
.IR slowControlVI NNN .log ,
where
.I NNN
is the three-digit calorimeter board ID.
The plugin writes them to the
.I slowControl/
subdirectory of the first element of
.BR MU2E_CALORIMETER_CONFIG_PATH .
.PP
The script works on the
.B current directory
only (the directory is hard-coded as
.IR ./ ),
so it must be run from inside that
.I slowControl/
directory.
It:
.IP 1. 4
truncates (or creates)
.I summary.log
and
.I summaryVI.log
in the current directory;
.IP 2. 4
appends the last line of every
.IR slowControl [0-9]*.log
to
.IR summary.log ,
and of every
.IR slowControlVI [0-9]*.log
to
.IR summaryVI.log ,
in
.B sort \-V
(board) order;
.IP 3. 4
copies the two summaries to
.IR summary_ YYYYmmdd_HHMM .log
and
.IR summaryVI_ YYYYmmdd_HHMM .log ;
.IP 4. 4
prints the names of the two dated copies, prefixed with the Italian
.RB \(lq "Creato riepilogo:" \(rq
(\(lqsummary created\(rq).
.PP
The script is installed with the rest of
.I boardConfig/
by the package's
.B install(DIRECTORY boardConfig ...)
rule.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
Arguments are ignored.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR slowControl NNN .log ", " slowControlVI NNN .log
Input: per-board logs written by the
.B ROC Slow Control
macro.
.TP
.IR summary.log ", " summaryVI.log
Output: overwritten on every run.
.TP
.IR summary_ YYYYmmdd_HHMM .log ", " summaryVI_ YYYYmmdd_HHMM .log
Output: dated copies.
A second run in the same minute overwrites them.
.TP
.I boardConfig/slowControl/.gitignore
Ignores
.IR *.log ,
so logs written into a source checkout are never committed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The script itself reads no environment variables.
.TP
.B MU2E_CALORIMETER_CONFIG_PATH
Read by the FE plugin, not by this script; its first colon-separated
element plus
.I /slowControl
is the directory to run the script in.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 0 in practice: the script does not use
.BR "set \-e" ,
so the exit status is that of the final
.BR echo .
A failed
.B cp
is reported on standard error but not in the exit status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Summarise the readings from a run of the
.B ROC Slow Control
macro:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cd "${MU2E_CALORIMETER_CONFIG_PATH%%:*}/slowControl"
bash slow_control_summary.sh
cat summary.log
.fi
.RE
.SH BUGS
File names are produced by an unquoted
.B $(ls ... | sort \-V)
loop, so a path containing whitespace would be split.
With no matching logs the summaries are empty and the script still
succeeds.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR otsdaq-mu2e-calorimeter-root-macros (7)
.PP
.I doc/INTERFACES.md
in the otsdaq-mu2e-calorimeter source tree, section 3.
.SH AUTHOR
Script by the Mu2e calorimeter group.
Manual page written for the September 2026 Mu2e DAQ review.
